  "lineage": "Punjabi rap grew from mid-2000s UK and Canadian diaspora records (Bohemia's Delhi-Punjabi Urdu rap, RDB's bhangra-rap fusions) into a mass Indian form after 2017 through Sidhu Moose Wala, Karan Aujla and the Brampton-Ludhiana production axis — 90-160 BPM tracks that graft trap 808s and half-time snares onto dhol chaal accents and tumbi riffs, with rapped or half-sung Punjabi verses in a hard, chest-forward register and lyric matter running from village pride to gangster narrative.",
